minor.recommendation:
Add a complementary per-email key:

  private static String forgotEmailKey(String email) { return "forgot:rate:email:" + email; }

  Mono<Boolean> emailLimit = redisTemplate.opsForValue()
      .setIfAbsent(forgotEmailKey(email), "1", FORGOT_RATE_TTL)
      .onErrorResume(err -> Mono.just(true));
  Mono<Boolean> ipLimit = redisTemplate.opsForValue()
      .setIfAbsent(forgotKey(ip), "1", FORGOT_RATE_TTL)
      .onErrorResume(err -> Mono.just(true));
  return Mono.zip(emailLimit, ipLimit)
      .flatMap(t -> (Boolean.FALSE.equals(t.getT1()) || Boolean.FALSE.equals(t.getT2()))
          ? Mono.empty() : doForgotPassword(email, ip, userAgent));

Keep silent over-limit handling (return 200 with no body) so timing remains uniform. The per-email key must be set BEFORE the user lookup (canonicalized email is what we have) so timing is independent of email validity.
